course: dictionary
lesson: 6948
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Context, the words and sentences around them, tells you which meaning the writer means. Painter is one of these words.
explain: «A punt is a flat-bottomed boat pushed along with a long pole on shallow rivers; a painter is the rope at the front of a boat used to tie it up.» Here the clues are boat, rope and tie it up, so painter is a rope, not a person. Always ask: which meaning fits this sentence?
explain: «Frida Kahlo, a Mexican painter, painted with a mirror above her bed.» The clue is painted: a painter is a person who paints pictures, an artist. When painter means a worker who paints the walls of a house, the sentence will mention walls, rooms or decorating instead.
fact: A painter is a person who paints pictures, an artist.
fact: A painter can also be a worker who paints walls, houses and buildings, as in «a painter and decorator».
fact: A painter on a boat is a rope at the front, used to tie it up. This meaning is rare.
fact: «Van Gogh painted a series of sunflower paintings» to decorate a room for his friend «the painter Paul Gauguin».
fact: Context clues help you choose the right meaning: swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
exercise: «A punt is a flat-bottomed boat; a painter is the rope at the front of a boat used to tie it up.» What is a painter in this sentence? | A person who paints pictures | *A rope used to tie a boat up | A worker who paints houses
exercise: «Frida Kahlo, a Mexican painter, painted with a mirror above her bed.» What is a painter in this sentence? | A kind of rope | A flat-bottomed boat | A worker who paints houses | *A person who paints pictures
exercise: «Kateryna Bilokur, a self-taught Ukrainian painter, painted incredibly detailed flowers.» Find and copy the word that shows what the painter did. | Ukrainian | *painted | self-taught | incredibly
test: «Van Gogh painted sunflowers for his friend the painter Paul Gauguin.» What does painter mean here? | *An artist who paints pictures | A flat-bottomed boat | A worker who paints walls | A rope at the front of a boat
test: Which meaning fits a painter who paints the walls of a house? | *A worker who paints walls, houses and buildings | A person who paints pictures | A rope used to tie a boat up | A long pole for pushing a punt
exam: Read: «a painter and decorator» is a job. What does a painter and decorator do? | Ties up boats on a river | *Paints walls and decorates houses | Writes stories for a gallery | Makes thousands of prints
